### Drill 4: Cluster Resource Telemetry (`04-metrics-monitoring/`)

A recurring CKA exam requirement is querying node and pod resource consumption (CPU and memory) to identify capacity
bottlenecks.

#### Step 1: Verify Metrics Server API

Ensure Metrics Server is collecting resource telemetry (if not deployed, run
`/home/vagrant/cka/helm/install-kube-metrics.sh`):

```bash
kubectl top nodes
kubectl top pods -A
```

#### Step 2: Sort by CPU and Memory Consumption

In the exam, quickly identify high-utilization workloads using the `--sort-by` flag:

```bash
# Find node with highest CPU utilization
kubectl top nodes --sort-by=cpu

# Find node with highest memory utilization
kubectl top nodes --sort-by=memory

# Identify top CPU-consuming pods cluster-wide
kubectl top pods -A --sort-by=cpu

# Identify top memory-consuming pods in a specific namespace
kubectl top pods -n kube-system --sort-by=memory
```

#### Step 3: Run Resource Telemetry Validation

```bash
cd {{ cka_lab_cluster_troubleshooting_dir }}/04-metrics-monitoring
./test-metrics-top.sh
```

